'''Lord of Ruin Jagando''' (破壊神ジャガンドー, ''Hakai-shin Jagandō'', '''Destruction God Jagando''') is an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemy found exclusively in an [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|invasion]] which appears in [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)|Mount Aku/Mount Fuji]] after clearing all stages in [[The Aku Realms]]. Once defeated, his [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] counterpart [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] will be unlocked. He was added in [[Version 10.9 Update|Version 10.9]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Lord of Ruin Jagando
|image = E 572.png
|appearance = '''Aku Realm:''' [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|Mount Aku/Mount Fuji Invasion]]
|money drop = 5,000¢ - 19,750¢
}}

==Enemy==
At a glance, Lord of Ruin Jagando may not seem that dangerous, as each of his first two hits of his attack deals only 6,000 damage, and the third takes much longer to execute. These major weaknesses are completely offset by an [[Omni Strike]] reaching the majority of units at up to 450, including [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]] that could help cut down his effective health pool of 5,600,000; while his reduced standing range at 300 removes any chance of him missing his third hit and allows him to move forward more easily. If that weren't enough, the third hit also carries a wildly inconsistent [[Surge Attack]] that has a 30% chance to spawn and could wipe out everything or nothing depending on when and where it appears; so don't expect to beat him and his support on your first try.

