==Trivia==
*As a skull-wearing demonic god of destruction summoned by an [[High Priest Mamon|evil priest]], he is more than likely a reference to the ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest|Dragon Quest]]'' character [[wikia:dragonquest:Malroth|Malroth]].
**The name Jagando (ジャガンドー) may be derived from 邪 ''ja'' (evil), ジャガーノート ''jagānōto'' (juggernaut) and シドー ''Shidō'' (Malroth's Japanese name).
*Jagando may have been inspired by the Hindu god of destruction, [[wikipedia:Shiva|Shiva]], who is often depicted with multiple pairs of arms and [https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:6_Śiva_and_Pārvatī_seated_on_a_terrace._1800_(circa)_BM.jpg blue skin]. Shiva's ''[[wikipedia:Vahana|vāhana]]'', [[wikipedia:Nandi (Hinduism)|Nandi]], is a bull, which may be referenced by the horns on Jagando's head. The skulls on Jagando's body could be based on the [[wikipedia:Mundamala|Mundamala]] (skull garland) worn by Shiva, and Jagando appearing on [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)|Mount Aku]] could be a reference to how Shiva resides on the mountain [[wikipedia:Kailasha|Kailasha]], where he meditates sitting in a lotus position, the same pose as the [[Media:Bg137.png|cat statue]] in the non-[[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|invaded]] version of Mount Aku.
*[[The Aku Realms]]' ending mentions that when the [[Cat Units|Cats]] defeated Jagando, he spit out an egg which hatched into [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] This is a reference to [[wikia:dragonball:King Piccolo|King Piccolo]] from ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Ball|Dragon Ball]]'', whose last action before dying was to spit out an egg containing his final child and reincarnation, Piccolo Jr.
*He is tied with [[High Priest Mamon]] for the highest [[Shield]] health of all Aku enemies.

